[CONTRADICTED] A3
  claim     : On f5 at N=5000 the V2-bank criterion floor is 0.0248 against a dictionary capability of 8e-17 - fourteen orders of magnitude.
  source    : diagnosis_report.md 3.1
  recomputed: the double-precision R_full* there is 8.33e-17, which sits AT the validated analytic-ISE resolution floor 1.3e-15 for that target. A 50-digit mpmath recomputation of the same optimum gives 2.11e-17, so the dictionary optimum is genuinely below 1e-16 - but the double-precision figure carries ~75% relative error and must not be quoted to two significant figures, let alone turned into an orders-of-magnitude statement. Report the absolute excess 0.02478 and an upper bound on R_full*.
  action    : Replace with: 'the 300-atom dictionary represents this target to an exact risk below 1e-16 (verified at 50-digit precision), while the V2-bank population-moment fit leaves 0.0248'. Give the absolute excess; do not quote a ratio against a value at the noise floor.

[CONTRADICTED] A4
  claim     : Replacing the estimated covariance by the population covariance changes results by well under 2x in every cell.
  source    : results_summary.md 3.2
  recomputed: as a RATIO the max over all 16 cells is 22.7 (f0 N=500, matched bank) and 3 of 16 cells exceed 2 - but the largest ratios occur where both rungs are at roundoff level (3.2e-07 vs 7.3e-06 there). Restricted to the 16 cells where both rungs exceed the analytic-ISE resolution floor, the max ratio is 22.73. As an ABSOLUTE change relative to that cell's total sampled moment error the substitution moves the result by at most 16.4% (median 1.59%).
  action    : Drop the blanket '<2x in every cell'. Report the absolute effect: estimating Omega rather than knowing it moves the population-moment fit by at most 16% of the cell's total error. Ratios computed at roundoff level must not be quoted.

